course: dictionary
lesson: 13421
title: Many meanings of hitting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Hitting» is one of them, so you need the words around it to know which meaning is right. Ask yourself: what is being hit, and why?
explain: «The bird kept hitting the window with its wings.» Here hitting means touching something hard and fast. «Maya was hitting the ball over the net.» Here hitting means striking a ball with a bat, racket or hand, as in sport.
explain: «Sam scored well in the test, hitting 100 out of 100.» Here hitting means reaching a number or a target. Each time, try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: «Hitting» is the -ing form of the verb «hit». The verb forms are hit, hits, hit, hitting.
fact: «Hitting» can mean touching something hard and fast, or striking a ball with a bat, racket or hand.
fact: «Hitting» can also mean reaching something, like a target or a score of 100.
fact: Hitting another person is never OK. Use words, walk away or tell an adult instead.
fact: «Hitting it off» means getting on well with someone. «Hitting the books» means studying hard.
exercise: «Lily was hitting the nail with the hammer.» What does hitting mean here? | Studying hard | *Touching something hard and fast | Getting on well with a friend | Reading the instructions carefully
exercise: «Ravi was hitting the ball with his bat during cricket practice.» What does hitting mean here? | *Striking the ball with a bat | Leaving the field early | Sleeping under a tree | Reading a book about cricket
exercise: Sam's friend says hitting is OK when someone is annoying. What should Sam do instead? | Hide the ball so nobody can play | *Use words, walk away or tell an adult | Hit him back, harder
test: «Zoe and Amir are hitting it off at school.» What does hitting it off mean? | Fighting each other | *Getting on well | Sleeping late | Hitting a ball very hard
test: «Tom spent all weekend hitting the books for his spelling test.» What does hitting the books mean? | Playing football all weekend | Going shopping | Hitting another player | *Studying hard
exam: «The arrow kept hitting the target.» What does hitting mean here? | *Reaching the target | Going home for lunch | Losing the arrow in the grass | Dropping the bow on the floor
